// Title: Arbitrary File Download Via MSEDGE_PROXY.EXE
// Sigma ID: e84d89c4-f544-41ca-a6af-4b92fd38b023
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel
// Date: 2023-11-09 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1218
// Description: Detects usage of "msedge_proxy.exe" to download arbitrary files
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/msedge_proxy/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_msedge_proxy_download.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\msedge_proxy.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "msedge_proxy.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "http://" or ProcessCommandLine contains "https://")
